using System.Threading.Tasks;

public static async IAsyncEnumerable<T> StreamResultsFromQueryAsync<T>(IEnumerable<FilterCriteria> filterCriteria, SqlConnection connection, string sqlCommand) 
{
    try
    {
        await connection.OpenAsync();

        using (var command = new SqlCommand(sqlCommand, connection))
        {
            foreach (var criteria in filterCriteria)
            {
                command.Parameters.AddWithValue(criteria.Name, criteria.Value);
            }

            using (var reader = await command.ExecuteReaderAsync())
            {
                while (await reader.ReadAsync())
                {
                    yield return (T)reader[0]; // Assuming T is same as the first column in your query result. Adjust this according to your actual data type and structure.
                }
            }
        }
    }
    catch(Exception ex)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Error occurred while streaming results: " + ex);
    }
    finally 
    {
        await connection.CloseAsync();
    }
}
```
This code creates a method that executes an SQL query and yields each row of the result as it is read from the database. It uses `yield return` to create an iterator, which allows you to process data on-the-fly without needing to load all the results into memory at once. The connection string and SQL command are passed as parameters to this method.
