        try {
            boolean acquired = lock.tryLock();
            if (acquired) {
                deleteFileIfExists(filePath);

                long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
                Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);
                int exitCode = process.waitFor();
                long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

                logger.info("Command executed with command: {}, filePath: {}, start time: {}, end time: {}, exit code: {}", cmd, filePath, startTime, endTime, exitCode);

                lock.unlock();
            } else {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Another thread is executing the command");
            }
        } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
            logger.error(String.format("Error while executing the command: %s", cmd), e);
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
    }

    private void deleteFileIfExists(String filePath) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        File file = new File(filePath);

        if (file.exists() && !file.delete()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Unable to delete the file: " + filePath);
        }
    }

    private String getEnvironmentVariableOrDefault(String key, String defaultValue) {
        return StringUtils.defaultIfBlank(System.getenv(key), defaultValue);
    }
}
```
This program uses a `ReentrantLock` to ensure thread-safe execution of the command and file deletion. It logs all command execution details for debugging and monitoring purposes. The program gets its environment variables using `java.lang.System#getenv()`, with a fallback value if it doesn't exist or is blank. This class uses Apache Commons Lang3 to handle null-safe comparison of strings when getting the environment variable value.
']

