['Here is the code for this task which follows best practices for dynamic memory management in C and handles all operational constraints mentioned above. It uses pthread library for thread safety, atomic operations for synchronization and time logging for performance analysis:

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <stdio.h>

// Define packet metadata structure
typedef struct {
    TRANSMIT_BUFFER_HEADER;
    PACKET_IDENTIFIER;
    TRANSMIT_STATUS_FLAGS;
} TX_PACKET_METADATA;

pthread_mutex_t allocator_lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER; // Mutex for thread safety
atomic_uint success_count = 0, failure_count = 0; // For statistics
struct timespec start_time, end_time; // For time logging
double total_time = 0.0; // Total time taken by allocations

// Function to manage memory allocation
TX_PACKET_METADATA* allocate_metadata(int n) {
    TX_PACKET_METADATA *array = NULL;

    clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &start_time); // Start time before allocation
    pthread_mutex_lock(&allocator_lock); // Lock for atomicity

    array = malloc(sizeof(TX_PACKET_METADATA) * n); 

    if (array == NULL) {
        perror("Memory allocation failed");
        atomic_fetch_add(&failure_count, 1); // Increment failure count
    } else {
        atomic_fetch_add(&success_count, 1); // Increment success count
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&allocator_lock); // Unlock after allocation
    clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &end_time); // End time after allocation
    total_time += (end_time.tv_sec - start_time.tv_sec) + (end_time.tv_nsec - start_time.tv_nsec) / 1e9; // Add to total time

    return array;
}

// Function to free memory
void deallocate_metadata(TX_PACKET_METADATA *array, int n) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&allocator_lock); // Lock before deallocation
    if (array != NULL) {
        free(array);
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&allocator_lock); // Unlock after deallocation
}

// Function to print statistics
void print_statistics() {
    printf("Memory allocation success rate: %.2f%%\n", 100 * (double)success_count / (failure_count + success_count));
    printf("Average memory allocation time: %.6fs\n", total_time / success_count);
}
```

This function allocates an array of TX_PACKET_METADATA structures and logs the start and end times for each allocation, which allows us to calculate average time per allocation. It also handles memory exhaustion by returning NULL when malloc fails. Statistics on success rates and average allocation times are calculated and printed.

The function is thread-safe as it uses a mutex for locking. This ensures that two threads cannot allocate memory at the same time, which could lead to data corruption or other unexpected behavior in a multi-threaded environment. It also handles potential race conditions between concurrent memory allocation requests by serializing access through the use of locks.
']

