    }));
}
for (auto& thread : threads) {
    thread.join();
}
``` 
This will create a separate thread for each iteration and generate a random number in each one. Note that this is just a very simple example, it doesn't handle the complexities mentioned in your question such as dynamically switching between different RNG algorithms and distribution types at runtime. These advanced features would require much more complex code to implement.
