This function uses `fs.promises` module, which provides asynchronous versions of common fs functions. The implementation is asynchronous from top to bottom - this means that if an error occurs while reading the file, we will catch it and log a detailed message before re-throwing the same error with a different message.

For memory usage optimization: Node.js reads files in chunks so it doesn't need to load whole file into memory at once, improving performance and minimizing memory usage when processing large files. 

