['Here is a simple representation of AsyncReduction in JavaScript.

```javascript
async function AsyncReduction(arr, initVal, callback) {
  let result = initVal;

  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; ++i) {
    try {
      result = await callback(result, arr[i]);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Error during callback execution:', err);
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

This function processes an array of numbers asynchronously by invoking a given callback for each element in the array, passing it a running total and the current element. If any errors occur during this process, they are caught and logged to the console. This way, even if a network request or computation-heavy task is involved, the function will not be interrupted.

Now let's implement the NetworkDataProcessor class in C#:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public class NetworkDataProcessor {
    private int _minValue, _maxValue;

    public NetworkDataProcessor(int minVal, int maxVal) {
        if (minVal > maxVal) { throw new ArgumentException("Min value must not be greater than Max value."); }

        this._minValue = minVal; 
        this._maxValue = maxVal;
    }

    public float GenerateRandomFloat() {
        Random rand = new Random();
        double val = rand.NextDouble(); // returns a random number between 0 and 1

        return (float) ((val * (_maxValue - _minValue)) + _minValue); // scales the number to the range
    }

    public int GenerateRandomInt() {
        Random rand = new Random();
        lock(rand) { // ensures thread safety
            return rand.Next(_minValue, _maxValue);
        }
    }

    public int GenerateExcludingMax() {
        Random rand = new Random();
        lock (rand) {
            int val;

            do {
                val = rand.Next(_minValue, _maxValue + 1); // +1 to include maxVal
            } while(val == _maxValue); // ensures the returned value is not equal to maxVal

            return val;
        }
    }

    public async Task ShuffleArrayAsync(int[] array) {
        Random rng = new Random();
        int n = array.Length;  

        while (n > 1) {  
          n--; 

          int k = rng.Next(n + 1);  
          int value = array[k];  
          array[k] = array[n];  
          array[n] = value;  
        }

        await Task.Delay(0); // simulate asynchronous operation for demonstration purposes
    }
}
```
This class generates random float, integer and excludes max values in a range of numbers. Also includes async method to shuffle an array which is efficient with large arrays. It uses thread-safe random instance and locks it to prevent race conditions when generating random number sequences. Note: the `ShuffleArrayAsync` function currently does not actually perform any I/O operations, it's just a simulation of an asynchronous operation for demonstration purposes.
']

