                list[j] = list[j + 1];  // Shift remaining elements
            }
            size--;
        }
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
```

This is just a basic overview and does not include external logging, performance monitoring tools integration or CPU and memory resource limitations. Also, proper error handling mechanism should be incorporated. For instance, the `add` function might fail if there's no more system memory available for expanding the list. Similarly, it would be good to check if `realloc` returned a non-null pointer to avoid potential problems with corrupted data.
