['This problem is quite complex and involves multiple considerations such as concurrency control, error handling, caching, logging, dynamic loading of strategies for different operation types, rate limiting, latency requirements, backpressure mechanism, etc. 

Here is a simple representation of `processUserRequests` in Java using some of the concepts discussed:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class UserRequestProcessor {

    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(UserRequestProcessor.class.getName());
    private static ConcurrentMap<Integer, Request> requestCache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>(); // Sample caching mechanism using ConcurrentHashMap

    public Map<String, Object> processUserRequests(int[] requestIds) {
        if (requestIds == null) return Collections.emptyMap();

        ExecutorService executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors()); // Create thread pool with size equal to the number of available processors
        Map<String, Object> report = new ConcurrentHashMap<>(); // Use concurrent map for shared access by multiple threads

        CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(requestIds.length); 
        long startTime = System.nanoTime();

        for (int requestId : requestIds) {
            executorService.execute(() -> {
                try {
                    processRequest(report, requestCache.computeIfAbsent(requestId, this::fetchRequest)); // Fetch and cache the request if not already cached 
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); // Restore the interruption status
                    logger.log(Level.WARNING, "Processing interrupted", e);
                } finally {
                    latch.countDown(); // Signal that a request has been processed
                }
            });
        }

        try {
            latch.await(); // Wait for all requests to be processed
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); // Restore the interruption status
            logger.log(Level.WARNING, "Processing interrupted", e);
        } finally {
            executorService.shutdownNow(); // Shut down the executor service to prevent resource leakage
            report.put("averageProcessingTimePerRequest",  (System.nanoTime() - startTime) / requestIds.length); // Calculate average processing time per request
        }

        return report;
    }

    private Request fetchRequest(int requestId) {
        // Fetch and return the request corresponding to the given id
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException();
    }

    private void processRequest(Map<String, Object> report, Request request) throws InterruptedException {
        // Perform operation based on type of user request
        if (request.getProcessingTime() > 1000) { // If processing time exceeds threshold, trigger alert mechanism
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "High processing time detected for requestId: " + request.getId());
        }
        report.compute("totalRequests", (k, v) -> v == null ? 1 : ((int)v + 1)); // Increment the total requests count
    }
}
```

Please note that this is a simplified representation and doesn't account for all the considerations mentioned in the problem. Also, dynamic loading of strategies, backpressure mechanism, error retry logic, rate limiting, cache invalidation strategy, latency requirements and other optimizations are out-of-scope for this simple example.
']

