['Java MD5 hashing method:
```java
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

public class Hashing {
    public static String md5Hash(String input) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        if (input == null || input.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input string cannot be null or empty");
        }

        MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
        byte[] messageDigest = md.digest(input.getBytes());
        StringBuilder hexString = new StringBuilder();

        for (byte b : messageDigest) {
            hexString.append(Integer.toHexString(0xFF & b));
        }

        return hexString.toString();
    }
}
```
C# AES decryption method:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;

public class Decryption {
    public static string Decrypt(string ciphertext, string key, string iv, string padding) {
        if (key == null || iv == null || padding == null) {
            throw new ArgumentNullException("Parameters cannot be null");
        }

        // Validate parameters for correctness before decryption.
        if (!ValidateKey(key)) {
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid key length, must be 128, 192 or 256 bits.");
        }

        if (!ValidateIV(iv)) {
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid IV length. Must be 16 bytes");
        }

        // Choose padding mode based on user preference.
        PaddingMode pad = ChoosePaddingMode(padding);

        using (AesCryptoServiceProvider aesAlgorithm = new AesCryptoServiceProvider()) {
            aesAlgorithm.Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(key);
            aesAlgorithm.IV = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(iv);
            aesAlgorithm.Padding = pad;

            ICryptoTransform decryptor = aesAlgorithm.CreateDecryptor(aesAlgorithm.Key, aesAlgorithm.IV);

            byte[] cipherTextBytes = Convert.FromBase64String(ciphertext);
            byte[] plainTextBytes = decryptor.TransformFinalBlock(cipherTextBytes, 0, cipherTextBytes.Length);

            return Encoding.UTF8.GetString(plainTextBytes);
        }
    }

    private static bool ValidateKey(string key) {
        int[] validSizes = new int[] {128, 192, 256};

        return Array.IndexOf(validSizes, key.Length * 8) >= 0;
    }

    private static bool ValidateIV(string iv) {
        return iv.Length == 16;
    }

    private static PaddingMode ChoosePaddingMode(string padding) {
        switch (padding.ToLower()) {
            case "pkcs7":
                return PaddingMode.PKCS7;
            case "ansix923":
                return PaddingMode.ANSIX923;
            case "iso10126":
                return PaddingMode.ISO10126;
            default:
                throw new ArgumentException("Invalid padding mode");
        }
    }
}
``` 
For caching, consider using Guava library or Caffeine which provides a powerful and flexible framework for caching in Java. For load balancing in the encryption service, you could use Netflix's Ribbon or AWS Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) depending on your environment. To monitor system performance, tools such as Prometheus or New Relic can be used.

To handle large volumes of data and high-frequency requests, consider implementing streaming processing and using non-blocking I/O operations where applicable. For AES decryption performance, consider optimizing the padding mode to provide the most efficient option based on typical use cases. 

Remember to write unit tests for each method and component to ensure correctness of functionality. Consider implementing a comprehensive logging system to track system events and errors. For future enhancements, you could implement support for external data sources and additional cryptographic standards. Also consider implementing an API Gateway or service mesh for managing communication between services and adding security features.
