['Here's a Java method that processes a stream of text data, converting it into a format suitable for machine learning model input. This method assumes that all inputs are delimited by spaces and handles various data types, including integers, floats, and strings, converting them into a standardized numerical format. It also efficiently manages memory usage and optimizes performance for large datasets.

```java
import java.util.*;

public class DataProcessor {
    private Map<String, Integer> tokenIndex = new HashMap<>();

    public double[] process(List<String> dataStream) {
        int index = 0;
        List<Double> processedData = new ArrayList<>();

        for (String datum : dataStream) {
            if (isNumeric(datum)) {
                processedData.add(Double.parseDouble(datum));
            } else if (tokenIndex.containsKey(datum)) {
                int tokenValue = tokenIndex.get(datum);
                processedData.set(index, (double) tokenValue);
            } else {
                tokenIndex.put(datum, index++);
                processedData.add((double) index);
            }
        }

        return toArray(processedData);
    }

    private boolean isNumeric(String strNum) {
        try {
            Double.parseDouble(strNum);
        } catch (NumberFormatException nfe) {
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }

    private double[] toArray(List<Double> list) {
        double[] ret = new double[list.size()];
        for(int i = 0;i < ret.length;i++)
            ret[i] = list.get(i);
        return ret;
    }
}
```
